From f2c8a2c731c3644d105d7ac67592da9c509ff669 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TekRantGaming <craigferels896@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 03:28:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Resolve: integer destination number formats for 32bpp formats

The 32bpp full resolve packed every format as normalized values, ignoring
the destination number format. Integer formats (8_8_8_8, 2_10_10_10,
16_16) now store the truncated biased color as an integer, signed values
in two's complement. Trials Evolution resolves its occlusion depth
pyramid as signed 16_16 and reads it on the CPU; with normalized packing
every texel saturated and the culler hid visible geometry.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
